heavy  burden."  III.  Superlatively  heavy — "  too  heavy  for  me."  IV.  Not 
immovable,  for  though  too  heavy  for  me,  yet  Jesus  bore  it. 

Verse  5. — "  Foolishness."  The  folly  of  sin.  Everything  that  a  man  has  to 
do  with  sin  shows  his  folly.  I.  Dallying  with  sin.  II.  Committing  it.  III.  Con 
tinuing  in  it.  IV.  Hiding  it.  V.  Palliating  it.— B.  Davies. 

Verse  6. — Conviction  of  sin.     Its  grief,  its  depth,  its  continuance. 

Verse  6. — "  /  go  mourning."  I.  Unlawful  reasons  for  mourning.  II.  Legitimate 
themes  for  sorrow.  III.  Valuable  alleviations  of  grief. 

Verse  9. — The  many  desires  of  God's  children  :  the  fact  that  God  understands 
them  even  when  unexpressed  ;  and  the  certainty  that  he  will  grant  them. 

Verse  9. — Omniscience,  a  source  of  consolation  to  the  desponding. 

